# 2025雅思核心词汇
# 领域: 留学国际课程
# 学科: 雅思
# 来源: 2025雅思核心词汇
# 描述: 雅思考试核心词汇与用法

{{知识点1}}{{abandon /əˈbændən/ v. 放弃；抛弃；放纵
词义: to leave sb/sth permanently; to give up
例句: The government has abandoned plans to build a new airport.
搭配: abandon hope 放弃希望 / abandon oneself to 沉溺于
同义: forsake, desert, relinquish
雅思场景: 社会话题、环境问题中常用，如 "abandon traditional practices"（放弃传统做法）}}

{{知识点2}}{{adequate /ˈædɪkwət/ adj. 足够的；适当的
词义: enough in quantity or good enough in quality
例句: The company failed to provide adequate training for new employees.
搭配: adequate time/water/supply 足够的时间/水/供应
反义: inadequate, insufficient
雅思场景: 高频出现在阅读和写作中，尤其教育和健康类话题}}

{{知识点3}}{{inevitable /ɪnˈevɪtəbl/ adj. 不可避免的；必然的
词义: certain to happen; impossible to avoid
例句: Climate change is an inevitable consequence of industrial pollution.
搭配: inevitable result/consequence 必然的结果
同义: unavoidable, inescapable
雅思场景: 写作Task 2议论文常用，用于表达趋势或结论}}

{{知识点4}}{{substantial /səbˈstænʃəl/ adj. 大量的；实质性的；重要的
词义: large in amount, value, or importance
例句: There has been a substantial increase in house prices over the past decade.
搭配: substantial amount/evidence/improvement 大量/实质性证据/显著改善
同义: significant, considerable, considerable
雅思场景: 写作图表题和议论文高频词，替换 important 和 big}}

{{知识点5}}{{comprehensive /ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv/ adj. 全面的；综合的
词义: including everything that is needed; complete
例句: The report provides a comprehensive analysis of the education system.
搭配: comprehensive review/study/plan 全面审查/综合研究/完整计划
反义: partial, incomplete
雅思场景: 学术类阅读和写作中频繁出现}}

{{知识点6}}{{controversial /ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃəl/ adj. 有争议的
词义: causing a lot of disagreement or discussion
例句: The new immigration policy has proved highly controversial.
搭配: controversial issue/decision/topic 有争议的问题/决定/话题
同义: debatable, contentious, divisive
雅思场景: 写作Task 2讨论类话题核心词}}

{{知识点7}}{{deteriorate /dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/ v. 恶化；退化
词义: to become worse in quality or condition
例句: His health deteriorated rapidly after the diagnosis.
搭配: deteriorate rapidly/sharply 急剧恶化
同义: decline, worsen, degrade
雅思场景: 健康、环境、经济类话题常用}}

{{知识点8}}{{elaborate /ɪˈlæbərət/ adj. 精心制作的；详尽的 /ɪˈlæbəreɪt/ v. 详细阐述
词义: adj. very detailed and complicated; v. to explain in more detail
例句: Could you elaborate on your proposal? / She wore an elaborate costume.
搭配: elaborate plan/scheme 精心设计的计划 / elaborate on 详细说明
雅思场景: 口语Part 3中考官常用 "Could you elaborate on that?"}}

{{知识点9}}{{enhance /ɪnˈhɑːns/ v. 提高；增强；增进
词义: to improve the quality, amount, or strength of sth
例句: Technology can enhance the learning experience for students.
搭配: enhance performance/quality/reputation 提高表现/质量/声誉
同义: improve, boost, augment
雅思场景: 写作中替代 improve 的高级词汇}}

{{知识点10}}{{fundamental /ˌfʌndəˈmentl/ adj. 根本的；基本的
词义: relating to the most basic part of sth; essential
例句: Access to clean water is a fundamental human right.
搭配: fundamental change/right/principle 根本变化/基本权利/基本原则
同义: essential, basic, core
雅思场景: 写作议论文中用于强调重要性}}

{{知识点11}}{{genuine /ˈdʒenjuɪn/ adj. 真正的；真实的；真诚的
词义: real; exactly what it appears to be; sincere
例句: She showed genuine concern for the welfare of her students.
搭配: genuine interest/concern/attempt 真正的兴趣/真诚的关心/真诚的尝试
同义: authentic, real, sincere
雅思场景: 口语和写作中表达真实性}}

{{知识点12}}{{hostile /ˈhɒstaɪl/ adj. 敌对的；不友好的
词义: unfriendly and aggressive; strongly opposed
例句: The local residents were hostile to the idea of a new motorway.
搭配: hostile environment/reaction 敌对环境/敌意反应
同义: antagonistic, unfriendly, opposed
雅思场景: 社会、政治类话题}}

{{知识点13}}{{implement /ˈɪmplɪment/ v. 实施；执行
词义: to put a decision, plan, or system into operation
例句: The government plans to implement new environmental regulations.
搭配: implement a policy/plan/strategy 实施政策/计划/策略
同义: execute, carry out, enforce
雅思场景: 写作Task 2中描述政策执行的高频词}}

{{知识点14}}{{increasingly /ɪnˈkriːsɪŋli/ adv. 越来越多地；日益
词义: more and more all the time
例句: It is becoming increasingly difficult to find affordable housing.
搭配: increasingly important/popular/difficult 越来越重要/流行/困难
雅思场景: 写作开头句和描述趋势的万能副词}}

{{知识点15}}{{inevitable /ɪˈnevɪtəbl/ 见知识点3，此处为legitimate /ləˈdʒɪtɪmət/ adj. 合法的；正当的
词义: conforming to the law or to rules; reasonable and acceptable
例句: The protesters claim they have a legitimate grievance.
搭配: legitimate concern/reason/right 正当的担忧/合理的理由/合法的权利
同义: lawful, valid, justified
雅思场景: 法律、社会公正类话题}}

{{知识点16}}{{manipulate /məˈnɪpjuleɪt/ v. 操纵；控制；巧妙处理
词义: to control or influence sb/sth cleverly or unfairly
例句: Advertisements can manipulate consumers into buying unnecessary products.
搭配: manipulate information/data/people 操纵信息/数据/人
同义: control, exploit, influence
雅思场景: 媒体、广告、社会话题中常见}}

{{知识点17}}{{negligible /ˈneɡlɪdʒəbl/ adj. 微不足道的；可以忽略的
词义: too slight or small in amount to be of importance
例句: The difference in performance was negligible.
搭配: negligible effect/impact/difference 微不足道的影响/差别
同义: insignificant, trivial, minor
雅思场景: 学术写作中描述数据对比}}

{{知识点18}}{{phenomenon /fɪˈnɒmɪnən/ n. 现象；非凡的人或事
词义: a fact or event that can be seen or experienced; an unusual event
例句: Global warming is a well-documented phenomenon.
搭配: natural/social/common phenomenon 自然/社会/常见现象
复数: phenomena
雅思场景: 学术类阅读和写作高频词}}

{{知识点19}}{{preliminary /prɪˈlɪmɪnəri/ adj. 初步的；预备的
词义: happening before a more important action or event
例句: Preliminary results suggest the treatment is effective.
搭配: preliminary results/investigation/stage 初步结果/预备调查/初期阶段
雅思场景: 学术研究和调查类话题}}

{{知识点20}}{{profound /prəˈfaʊnd/ adj. 深刻的；意义深远的
词义: very great or intense; showing great knowledge or insight
例句: The internet has had a profound impact on the way we communicate.
搭配: profound effect/impact/influence 深远的影响
同义: deep, significant, far-reaching
雅思场景: 写作中表达影响程度的高级词汇}}

{{知识点21}}{{reluctant /rɪˈlʌktənt/ adj. 不情愿的；勉强的
词义: unwilling and hesitant; not wanting to do sth
例句: Many young people are reluctant to discuss their mental health.
搭配: reluctant to admit/accept/change 不情愿承认/接受/改变
同义: unwilling, hesitant, resistant
雅思场景: 社会心理类话题}}

{{知识点22}}{{rigid /ˈrɪdʒɪd/ adj. 严格的；僵硬的；死板的
词义: strict and difficult to change; stiff
例句: The school has a rigid system of rules and regulations.
搭配: rigid rules/structure/control 严格的规则/僵硬的结构
同义: strict, inflexible, stringent
反义: flexible, adaptable
雅思场景: 教育、管理类话题}}

{{知识点23}}{{simultaneously /ˌsɪmlˈteɪniəsli/ adv. 同时地
词义: at the same time
例句: The concert was broadcast simultaneously in 20 countries.
搭配: occur/happen simultaneously 同时发生
雅思场景: 描述流程或多任务场景}}

{{知识点24}}{{skeptical /ˈskeptɪkəl/ adj. 怀疑的
词义: having doubts; not easily convinced
例句: Many scientists remain skeptical about the effectiveness of the drug.
搭配: skeptical of/about 对…持怀疑态度
同义: doubtful, unconvinced, dubious
雅思场景: 科学研究、社会讨论类话题}}

{{知识点25}}{{spontaneous /spɒnˈteɪniəs/ adj. 自发的；自然的；即兴的
词义: happening naturally; not planned or organized
例句: The crowd broke into spontaneous applause.
搭配: spontaneous reaction/generation 自发的反应/自然产生
同义: impulsive, unplanned, natural
反义: planned, deliberate
雅思场景: 口语中描述性格或事件}}

{{知识点26}}{{sufficient /səˈfɪʃənt/ adj. 足够的；充分的
词义: enough for a particular purpose
例句: There was not sufficient evidence to convict the suspect.
搭配: sufficient time/evidence/reason 足够的时间/证据/理由
同义: enough, adequate, ample
雅思场景: 学术写作中表达数量或程度}}

{{知识点27}}{{undermine /ˌʌndəˈmaɪn/ v. 逐渐削弱；暗中破坏
词义: to make sth gradually weaker or less effective
例句: Constant criticism can undermine a child's confidence.
搭配: undermine authority/confidence/efforts 削弱权威/信心/努力
同义: weaken, sabotage, subvert
雅思场景: 写作Task 2中描述负面影响}}

{{知识点28}}{{versatile /ˈvɜːsətaɪl/ adj. 多才多艺的；多功能的
词义: able to do many different things; having many uses
例句: She is a versatile actress who can play both comedy and drama.
搭配: versatile tool/player/artist 多功能工具/全能选手/多才多艺的艺术家
雅思场景: 人物描述、产品介绍类话题}}

{{知识点29}}{{vulnerable /ˈvʌlnərəbl/ adj. 脆弱的；易受伤害的
词义: weak and easily hurt physically or emotionally
例句: Children are particularly vulnerable to the effects of air pollution.
搭配: vulnerable to 对…脆弱/易受…影响
同义: susceptible, exposed, defenseless
雅思场景: 健康、社会保护、环境类话题}}

{{知识点30}}{{widespread /ˈwaɪdspred/ adj. 广泛的；普遍的
词义: existing or happening over a large area or among many people
例句: There is widespread concern about the impact of social media.
搭配: widespread use/belief/concern 广泛使用/普遍看法/广泛关注
同义: prevalent, extensive, pervasive
雅思场景: 社会现象描述的高频词}}

{{知识点31}}{{alleviate /əˈliːvieɪt/ v. 减轻；缓解
词义: to make pain, suffering, or problems less severe
例句: The new policy aims to alleviate poverty in rural areas.
搭配: alleviate pain/suffering/poverty 减轻痛苦/缓解贫困
同义: relieve, ease, mitigate
雅思场景: 医疗、社会政策类话题}}

{{知识点32}}{{compulsory /kəmˈpʌlsəri/ adj. 强制的；义务的
词义: required by law or a rule; obligatory
例句: Education is compulsory for all children between the ages of 5 and 16.
搭配: compulsory education/attendance/subject 义务教育/强制出勤/必修科目
同义: mandatory, obligatory, required
反义: optional, voluntary
雅思场景: 教育政策类话题}}

{{知识点33}}{{consensus /kənˈsensəs/ n. 共识；一致意见
词义: a general agreement among a group of people
例句: There is a growing consensus that climate change is a serious threat.
搭配: reach a consensus/achieve consensus 达成共识
同义: agreement, accord, unanimity
雅思场景: 讨论、辩论、学术写作常用}}

{{知识点34}}{{crucial /ˈkruːʃəl/ adj. 至关重要的；关键的
词义: extremely important; of great importance
例句: Education plays a crucial role in reducing inequality.
搭配: crucial role/factor/decision 关键角色/因素/决定
同义: vital, essential, critical
雅思场景: 写作Task 2中强调重要性的必备词}}

{{知识点35}}{{cumulative /ˈkjuːmjələtɪv/ adj. 累积的；渐增的
词义: increasing by one addition after another
例句: The cumulative effect of years of pollution has devastated the river.
搭配: cumulative effect/impact 累积效应
雅思场景: 环境、健康类话题中描述长期影响}}

{{知识点36}}{{daunting /ˈdɔːntɪŋ/ adj. 令人畏惧的；令人气馁的
词义: seeming difficult to deal with; intimidating
例句: The prospect of starting a new life in a foreign country can be daunting.
搭配: daunting task/challenge/prospect 令人畏惧的任务/挑战
同义: intimidating, formidable, discouraging
雅思场景: 口语Part 2描述经历时常用}}

{{知识点37}}{{discernible /dɪˈsɜːnəbl/ adj. 可辨别的；看得见的
词义: able to be seen, noticed, or understood
例句: There was no discernible difference between the two products.
搭配: discernible difference/change/effect 可辨别差异/变化
同义: noticeable, detectable, visible
雅思场景: 学术写作中描述观察结果}}

{{知识点38}}{{empirical /ɪmˈpɪrɪkəl/ adj. 经验主义的；以实验为根据的
词义: based on observation and experiment rather than theory
例句: The theory lacks empirical evidence to support it.
搭配: empirical evidence/research/data 经验证据/实证研究
雅思场景: 学术研究和科学类阅读高频词}}

{{知识点39}}{{exacerbate /ɪɡˈzæsəbeɪt/ v. 使恶化；使加剧
词义: to make a problem, bad situation, or negative feeling worse
例句: The drought was exacerbated by deforestation.
搭配: exacerbate the problem/situation/tension 使问题/局势恶化
同义: worsen, aggravate, intensify
雅思场景: 环境、社会问题类写作中替代 make worse}}

{{知识点40}}{{feasible /ˈfiːzəbl/ adj. 可行的；可能的
词义: possible and practical to do; likely to be achieved
例句: Is it feasible to complete the project within six months?
搭配: feasible solution/option/plan 可行的解决方案/方案
同义: viable, practicable, achievable
反义: impractical, unfeasible
雅思场景: 讨论解决方案和建议时常用}}

{{知识点41}}{{hierarchical /ˌhaɪəˈrɑːkɪkəl/ adj. 等级制度的；层级的
词义: arranged in a hierarchy; relating to a system of ranking
例句: The company has a very rigid hierarchical structure.
搭配: hierarchical structure/system/organization 层级结构/等级制度
雅思场景: 管理、社会结构类话题}}

{{知识点42}}{{indispensable /ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl/ adj. 不可或缺的
词义: absolutely necessary; essential
例句: Clean water is indispensable for human survival.
搭配: indispensable part/role/tool 不可或缺的部分/角色/工具
同义: essential, vital, necessary
雅思场景: 强调重要性时替代 important}}

{{知识点43}}{{integrity /ɪnˈteɡrəti/ n. 正直；完整性
词义: the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles
例句: He is a man of great integrity and honesty.
搭配: personal/professional integrity 个人/职业操守
同义: honesty, morality, principle
雅思场景: 人物品质描述、商业道德类话题}}

{{知识点44}}{{mitigate /ˈmɪtɪɡeɪt/ v. 缓和；减轻
词义: to make sth less harmful, serious, or painful
例句: Trees can help mitigate the effects of climate change.
搭配: mitigate risks/effects/damage 降低风险/减轻影响
同义: alleviate, reduce, lessen
雅思场景: 环境、风险管理类学术写作}}

{{知识点45}}{{paradox /ˈpærədɒks/ n. 矛盾；悖论
词义: a situation that seems strange because it involves two opposite facts
例句: It's a paradox that the richest country has the poorest people.
搭配: apparent paradox 似乎矛盾的现象
雅思场景: 哲学、社会讨论类阅读和口语}}

{{知识点46}}{{pragmatic /præɡˈmætɪk/ adj. 务实的；实用主义的
词义: solving problems in a practical and sensible way
例句: We need a pragmatic approach to dealing with this crisis.
搭配: pragmatic approach/solution/way 务实的方法/解决方案
同义: practical, realistic, sensible
雅思场景: 讨论解决方案时常用}}

{{知识点47}}{{unprecedented /ʌnˈpresɪdentɪd/ adj. 史无前例的；空前的
词义: never done or known before
例句: The pandemic caused unprecedented disruption to global economies.
搭配: unprecedented growth/change/crisis 空前的增长/变化/危机
雅思场景: 重大事件描述，近年来在新闻和写作中高频出现}}

{{知识点48}}{{accountability /əˌkaʊntəˈbɪləti/ n. 责任；问责制
词义: the fact of being responsible for your actions
例句: There must be greater accountability in government spending.
搭配: hold sb accountable/make sb accountable 追究责任
雅思场景: 政治、管理、教育类话题}}

{{知识点49}}{{autonomous /ɔːˈtɒnəməs/ adj. 自治的；自主的
词义: having the ability to govern itself or control its own affairs
例句: The university is an autonomous institution with its own governing body.
搭配: autonomous region/vehicle/decision 自治区/自动驾驶/自主决定
同义: independent, self-governing, sovereign
雅思场景: 科技（自动驾驶）、政治类话题}}

{{知识点50}}{{sustainable /səˈsteɪnəbl/ adj. 可持续的
词义: able to continue for a long time without damaging the environment
例句: We need to find sustainable solutions to the energy crisis.
搭配: sustainable development/growth/energy 可持续发展/增长/能源
反义: unsustainable
雅思场景: 环境、经济类话题的超高频词，写作必备}}
